title: April 10, 1985: The Final Stretch
scene-id: start
is-card: true

= April 10, 1985 — Lima, Peru

Four days remain until the presidential election. Across Peru, campaign fever has reached its peak. Thirty-six-year-old Alan García and APRA lead comfortably in the polls, but the outgoing Belaúnde administration is collapsing under the weight of hyperinflation, labor strikes, and Sendero Luminoso attacks.

Inside APRA headquarters, the campaign committee convenes for its final strategy briefing. 

"The presidency is within our reach," García says, tapping the table. "But these final days will set the tone for how we govern. What is our primary campaign focus for this final push?"

- @focus_rally: Organize a massive closing rally in Lima emphasizing popular economic relief.
- @focus_moderates: Court moderate voters and business leaders concerned about fiscal stability.
- @focus_security: Focus campaign messaging on anti-terrorism and national security.
